{"id": "2026-10-25-news-racist-shooting-suspect-sent-to-psychiatric-watc", "date": "2026-10-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Racist shooting suspect sent to psychiatric watch", "summary": "French anti-terror prosecutors moved the suspect in the 23 October racist shooting in Trappes, which killed one and wounded five, to psychiatric observation.", "url": "https://www.elysee.fr/emmanuel-macron/2026/10/23/deplacement-a-trappes", "source_domain": "elysee.fr", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["security", "politics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "French anti-terrorism prosecutors (PNAT) said on Sunday 25 October that the man suspected of Friday's racist shooting in Trappes, west of Paris, had been moved from police custody to psychiatric observation, and that a blood test found cannabis and cocaine. On the morning of Friday 23 October, starting around 10:00, the gunman fired bursts from his car in the streets of Trappes and neighbouring La Verrière (Yvelines). He killed Pengo Bossio Wangi, a 26-year-old mixed martial arts (MMA) fighter from Poissy, and wounded five people, including a 12-year-old girl hit by eight bullets who is still in critical condition. The suspect, named as Kévin T., 39, told police he had targeted \"Black people and Arabs\" and said he had \"avenged the shopkeepers\" whose shops were looted during the 17 October riots, according to Le Monde as relayed by RFI. Investigators found a copy of Mein Kampf at his home, which he had booby-trapped with gas canisters wired to a timer. The PNAT opened a terrorism investigation for murder and attempted murder on grounds of race or religion. Visiting Trappes on Friday evening, President Emmanuel Macron called it \"a racist terrorist attack\" and \"a turning point in the life of our Republic and our Nation\". The psychiatric observation can last 48 hours and pauses the custody clock; it is meant to establish whether he is fit to be questioned.", "why": "prosecutors are treating it as racist terrorism, and the suspect himself linked it to last week's looting, which ties the attack to the protest wave now dividing France.", "thread_id": "2026-10-25-news-racist-shooting-suspect-sent-to-psychiatric-watc", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-25", "event_date": "2026-10-23", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["France", "Trappes", "PNAT", "Emmanuel Macron"]}
{"id": "2026-10-25-news-france-s-second-protest-day-stays-largely-calm", "date": "2026-10-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "France's second protest day stays largely calm", "summary": "About 410,000 people (800,000 per the CGT) marched across France on 24 October with limited clashes.", "url": "https://www.rts.ch/info/monde/2026/article/france-70-000-policiers-pour-la-journee-de-mobilisation-29395161.html", "source_domain": "rts.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing since 2026-10-17"], "topics": ["politics", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "France's second national day of cost-of-living protests, on Saturday 24 October, drew 410,000 people according to the interior ministry, or 800,000 according to the CGT union, and passed off far more calmly than the riots of 17 October. Paris police counted 110,000 marchers in the capital, and the CGT 250,000. Clashes broke out on the fringes in Paris, Marseille, Toulouse, Nice, Tours and Nantes, but on a much smaller scale than the previous weekend. In Paris, police said \"more than 500\" rioters attacked officers on the cours de Vincennes and used a water cannon and tear gas. Around 10,000 people marched in Lyon although no march had been authorised there. The government deployed 70,000 police and gendarmes; the Louvre and Orsay museums stayed closed, and a 23:00–06:00 curfew around Place de la République and Les Halles was extended until Monday 26 October. Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez said the marches had \"gone well\". The movement began with secondary-school pupils protesting about teacher shortages in late September and has since widened to fuel prices, wages and public services; on 17 October alone 2,400 people were arrested.", "why": "the turnout shows the movement has not faded after last week's violence, and pressure now shifts to the government's response.", "thread_id": "2026-10-25-news-france-s-second-protest-day-stays-largely-calm", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-25", "event_date": "2026-10-24", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["France", "CGT", "Laurent Nuñez"]}
{"id": "2026-10-25-news-brazil-votes-in-tight-lula-bolsonaro-runoff", "date": "2026-10-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Brazil votes in tight Lula–Bolsonaro runoff", "summary": "Brazil holds its presidential runoff between Lula and Flávio Bolsonaro on 25 October, with polls too close to call.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-votes-in-tight-runoff-between-leftist-lula-and-right-wing-flavio-bolsonaro/a-79753924", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing since 2026-10-04"], "topics": ["politics", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Brazilians vote on Sunday 25 October in the presidential runoff between President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva, 80, and Senator Flávio Bolsonaro, with the final polls too close to call. In the first round on Sunday 4 October, Bolsonaro took 47% to Lula's 45%, beating the polls. The last Datafolha and Quaest surveys put the gap inside the margin of error, and Datafolha's previous poll had them level at 50% each. Lula, first elected in 2002 and back in office since the 2022 election, is seeking a fourth term on his social and anti-poverty record. Bolsonaro, the eldest son of former president Jair Bolsonaro, is campaigning on crime and has said he would free his father, who is under house arrest after being convicted over a coup attempt in 2022. Political scientist Cláudio Couto told RFI that the number of undecided voters rose as the vote approached.", "why": "the result decides whether Latin America's largest country stays with a left-wing government that has clashed with Donald Trump over trade, or turns right under a candidate allied with Washington.", "thread_id": "2026-10-25-news-brazil-votes-in-tight-lula-bolsonaro-runoff", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-25", "event_date": "2026-10-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Brazil", "Lula", "Flávio Bolsonaro", "Jair Bolsonaro"]}
{"id": "2026-10-25-news-israel-to-seal-west-bank-on-election-day", "date": "2026-10-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Israel to seal West Bank on election day", "summary": "Israel's army will close all West Bank crossings on its 27 October election day after displacing about 2,000 Palestinians in Hebron.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/25/israel-to-close-occupied-west-bank-crossings-as-hebron-lockdown-continues", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing since 2026-10-23", "single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Israel's army said on Sunday 25 October that it will close all land crossings into and out of the occupied West Bank on Tuesday 27 October, the day of Israel's general election, and bar Palestinian workers from most areas from Sunday through Monday. The announcement follows a lockdown of Hebron, where Defence Minister Israel Katz confirmed that \"about 2,000\" Palestinians had been forced from their homes; Hebron's mayor, Yousef al-Ja'bari, put the number at 2,200. Katz told the broadcaster Kan they would not be allowed back \"until we've finished dealing with all the Hamas issues in Hebron\". The Israeli army has carried out hundreds of raids since Friday's attack in Hebron, which killed two Israeli soldiers and both Palestinian gunmen. The Palestinian Authority called the demolitions and displacements \"collective punishment\". About 200,000 Palestinians live in Hebron city.", "why": "Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, in a tight race on Tuesday 27 October, has spoken of an operation on a scale not seen since 1967, and the closures cut the territory off during the vote.", "thread_id": "2026-10-25-news-israel-to-seal-west-bank-on-election-day", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-25", "event_date": "2026-10-27", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Israel", "West Bank", "Hebron", "Israel Katz", "Benjamin Netanyahu"]}
{"id": "2026-10-25-news-saudi-arabia-intercepts-ten-houthi-missiles", "date": "2026-10-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Saudi Arabia intercepts ten Houthi missiles", "summary": "Saudi forces said they intercepted ten Houthi ballistic missiles on 25 October as Riyadh airport was due to reopen.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/10/25/l-arabie-saoudite-dit-avoir-intercepte-dix-missiles-lances-par-les-houthistes-vers-le-sud-du-pays_6800066_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing since 2026-10-08", "single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Saudi forces said they intercepted ten ballistic missiles fired by Yemen's Houthis toward the south of the kingdom early on Sunday 25 October, the day Riyadh's King Khalid International Airport was due to reopen after a two-week closure. The claim came from the Saudi-led coalition's spokesman, Turki Al-Maliki, in a post on X. Three explosions were heard in Riyadh on Sunday morning after official alert messages, AFP reported, and it was unclear whether the airport had resumed flights. Houthi military spokesman Yahya Saree said on Saturday that the group had again targeted the airport, and on Sunday warned airlines that it is \"a military target\" and that Riyadh would \"bear the consequences\" if it reopened. The Iran-backed Houthis and the Saudi-led coalition backing Yemen's government have traded strikes almost daily since the conflict resumed in July; a strike on a passenger terminal earlier this month killed 13 people and shut the airport. Neither side's claims can be independently verified.", "why": "Le Monde notes that attacks on Riyadh on this scale are unprecedented since Yemen's war began in 2014, and the Houthis are now openly threatening civil aviation in the Saudi capital.", "thread_id": "2026-10-25-news-saudi-arabia-intercepts-ten-houthi-missiles", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-25", "event_date": "2026-10-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Saudi Arabia", "Houthis", "Yemen", "King Khalid International Airport"]}
{"id": "2026-10-25-news-bulgaria-picks-a-president-amid-black-sea-strike", "date": "2026-10-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Bulgaria picks a president amid Black Sea strikes", "summary": "Bulgaria votes for president on 25 October; Moscow-leaning incumbent Iotova leads pro-Western Gyurov, with a 1 November runoff if needed.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-holds-presidential-elections-amid-divisions-over-ukraine-war/a-79753496", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics", "geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Bulgarians are voting on Sunday 25 October in a presidential election in which incumbent Iliana Iotova, who favours dialogue with Moscow and opposes military aid to Kyiv, leads pro-Western former caretaker prime minister Andrey Gyurov. Polls cited by DW put Iotova at 41–47% and Gyurov at 28–31%, with Kostadin Kostadinov of the pro-Russian Vazrazhdane (Revival) party third on 10–13%. If no one wins a majority, a runoff follows on Sunday 1 November. Iotova became acting president in January when Rumen Radev resigned to run in the parliamentary election, which he won; he is now prime minister. The presidency is largely ceremonial, but the president commands the armed forces, can veto laws and appoints caretaker governments in a crisis. The campaign was overshadowed by drone attacks on merchant ships off Bulgaria's coast this month; Radev's government has not blamed Russia directly, though he said the strikes \"benefit the Russian Federation\".", "why": "an Iotova win would strengthen Radev's Moscow-leaning line in an EU and NATO state on the Black Sea front.", "thread_id": "2026-10-25-news-bulgaria-picks-a-president-amid-black-sea-strike", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-25", "event_date": "2026-10-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Bulgaria", "Iliana Iotova", "Andrey Gyurov", "Rumen Radev"]}
{"id": "2026-10-25-news-starlink-restored-as-musk-accuses-ukraine", "date": "2026-10-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Starlink restored as Musk accuses Ukraine", "summary": "Ukraine said Starlink and Starshield were back at full speed on 24 October; Musk claimed Ukraine violated Starlink's terms, which Ukrainian officials deny.", "url": "https://kyivindependent.com/starshield-operations-restored-above-400-km-h-ukraines-defense-ministry-says/", "source_domain": "kyivindependent.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["disputed", "single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "tech"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Ukraine said on Saturday 24 October that the Starlink satellite network and its military version, Starshield, were back at full speed after more than a week of restrictions, and Elon Musk replied that Ukraine had broken Starlink's terms of service. For terminals on the move, the speed cap had been 161 km/h; Ukraine's defence ministry said connections were stable again above 400 km/h, which matters for units and drones operating on the move. President Volodymyr Zelensky thanked the US administration and Congress. Musk then wrote on X that Ukraine's military had \"used it for offensive drone strikes to kill people\" and that \"that loophole was closed last week\". Former defence-ministry adviser Serhii Sternenko and presidential adviser Serhii Beskrestnov denied this, saying moving terminals only work when registered on the military Starshield system. Musk also wrote that \"were Starlink to be turned off, the Ukrainian front line would collapse immediately\".", "why": "Ukraine's front-line communications depend on one private network, and its owner is now publicly setting conditions on how Kyiv's army may use it.", "thread_id": "2026-10-25-news-starlink-restored-as-musk-accuses-ukraine", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-25", "event_date": "2026-10-24", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ukraine", "Starlink", "Starshield", "Elon Musk"]}
{"id": "2026-10-25-news-bern-weighs-delaying-electric-car-levy", "date": "2026-10-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Bern weighs delaying electric-car levy", "summary": "The Federal Council is examining delaying or phasing in the planned 2030 electric-car levy, the NZZ am Sonntag reported.", "url": "https://www.nzz.ch/schweiz/e-autos-erleben-gerade-einen-boom-nun-duerfen-die-kaeufer-auf-eine-gnadenfrist-bei-den-steuern-hoffen-ld.10041677", "source_domain": "nzz.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Federal Council is examining whether to push back the planned levy on electric cars, now due in 2030, or phase it in gradually, according to its current financial plan, the NZZ am Sonntag reported on Sunday 25 October. The levy, proposed by transport minister Albert Rösti last autumn, is meant to replace the fuel tax that electric-car drivers do not pay, and would average about CHF 600 a year per car, or more than CHF 1,000 for high-mileage drivers. According to the paper, one option under discussion is to charge the full levy only from 2035, with a transitional charge from 2031 set at first at one-third and then two-thirds of the full amount. The Federal Roads Office (FEDRO) would not give details, saying only that the Federal Council should send the bill to parliament this year and decide the start date then. More than one in three new cars sold in September was fully electric, a record.", "why": "the NZZ says a delay could quickly save electric-car owners several hundred francs a year, at a cost of billions to the federal roads budget.", "thread_id": "2026-10-25-news-bern-weighs-delaying-electric-car-levy", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-25", "event_date": "2026-10-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Council", "FEDRO", "Albert Rösti"]}
{"id": "2026-10-25-news-martigny-prison-to-hold-vaud-inmates", "date": "2026-10-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Martigny prison to hold Vaud inmates", "summary": "Valais will reopen Martigny prison for 20 Vaud detainees, with Vaud paying CHF 750,000 to ease overcrowding.", "url": "https://www.rts.ch/info/regions/valais/2026/article/la-prison-de-martigny-va-rouvrir-pour-20-detenus-vaudois-29395451.html", "source_domain": "rts.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Valais will reopen the prison in Martigny, closed for nearly a decade, to hold 20 detainees from Vaud, RTS reported on Saturday 24 October. Vaud is paying the full CHF 750,000 needed to bring the building up to current standards. Vaud state councillor Vassilis Venizelos called it \"a transitional solution\" that will not solve the canton's prison overcrowding; Vaud plans 60 more places at Orbe and 410 by 2032.", "why": "it shows how short Vaud is of prison places, after Jura's parliament rejected a similar shared prison with Geneva in September.", "thread_id": "2026-10-25-news-martigny-prison-to-hold-vaud-inmates", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-25", "event_date": "2026-10-24", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Vaud", "Valais", "Martigny", "Vassilis Venizelos"]}
{"id": "2026-10-25-news-listeria-found-in-lidl-smoked-trout", "date": "2026-10-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Listeria found in Lidl smoked trout", "summary": "The FSVO warned on 24 October against eating Nautica smoked trout fillets sold by Lidl Schweiz after listeria was found.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/Zu55ei26MNhh", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "health"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The Federal Food Safety and Veterinary Office (FSVO) warned on Saturday 24 October against eating Nautica plain smoked trout fillets sold by Lidl Schweiz, after listeria bacteria were found in them. Lidl has withdrawn the product and ordered a recall. Listeria usually causes mild or no symptoms in healthy people, but it can be dangerous for newborns, older people, pregnant women and people with weak immune systems.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-25-news-listeria-found-in-lidl-smoked-trout", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-25", "event_date": "2026-10-24", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["FSVO", "Lidl Schweiz"]}
